{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1503644-moon-bridges-synchronization-how-the-garou-do-it","id":1503644,"title":"Moon Bridges synchronization. How the Garou do it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-21T16:37:12-08:00","id":1503644,"title":"Moon Bridges synchronization. How the Garou do it?","content":"How do they happen? I've scoured the books and there isn't a solid answer, the Player Books mentioned emissaries sent by the Gatekeeper but still don't have any information on how they enact the rites at the same time to establish the connection for the first time/to renew it. Maybe a talen to alert them about the rite given by the emissary? I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T16:45:15-08:00","id":1503645,"title":"","content":"If the emissaries have a packmate on each side, and the pack-link Totem benefit... well that solves the communication issue right there. They can mentally communicate to keep both sides on schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:24:13-08:00","id":1503653,"title":"","content":"Nowadays you can use clocks and watches to coordinate. In the past, you can use the stars to tell time. You can use the position of the Big Dipper as it revolves around the North Star as a crude 24 hour clock. Astronomy has always been useful in determining both the time and location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T05:49:58-08:00","id":1503676,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms' answer was surprisingly simple indeed, wow, never thought of that.<br /> <br /> I thank Black Fox also. The Caern totem and the Gatekeeper can maintain constant communication so they could also inform each other about stars' positions. This would solve rites in the same time zones. But using the stars in the past for different time zones I suppose it would require what Heavy Arms said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","user":"Fenixpp","date":". 02-22-2023, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T13:08:16-08:00","id":1503698,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want to coordinate in different time zones, all the other time zone needs to do is take into effect the time difference on their clock (whether it is a real clock, or using something like the North Start / Big Dipper clock).<br /> <br /> Now you will never get a perfect alignment because even within the same time zone, different longitudes will be aligned differently. But the Rite of the Opened Caern is a level four right which means it takes at least forty minutes to perform. I would hold that it is less that each rite must be done simultaneously (meaning the rites at each caern must be started the same) and more like they must overlap each other. And there is nothing saying that the rite must end after forty minutes. Why can't the rite last longer if needed? That would give each sept more time to make sure that the rites are overlapping. So maybe it takes place over sixty or even ninety minutes.<br /> <br /> Now the Rite of the Open Caern and having moonbridges between various septs is not supposed to be a hard thing. Yeah, it should take effort, but I don't think it should be something that requires ridiculous logistics. It should be something the Garou can do during the Stone Age even with caerns far away from each other. It should not require phones or having members of a pack already travelled to the other caern so they can communicate with each other. Moonbridges are supposed to be a special type of Lune, and are formed by Pathstones/Moongems provided by Luna. And the moon as a celestial object helps tell time. So all of these are corresponding to each other. So if we really want each sept to know that the other sept has also &quot;matched&quot; their rite with each other, I would have the Pathstones at each caern glow or shimmer or give off some clue that the two septs are aligned while in the midst of the rite, and that a significant part of each rite - say twenty or thirty minutes - of the pathstones being &quot;aligned&quot; is part of what is needed during the rite to create the Moonbridge. Using the pathstone/moongem in this way eliminates the need for additional talens or fetishes and keeps things simple since it is already a required part of the rite, and it makes spiritual sense since all pathstones come from the same source, Luna.<br /> <br /> To me that makes sense and makes it easy so this isn't harder than it should be. Some time before they need to renew (or create a brand new) the Moonbridge, each Sept send over a Moonwalker (the assistant tot he Gatekeeper who must stay at the caern) to the other caern. They hammer out the details of when each sept will perform the rite - they agree on the date, the approximate time at each sept for the rite to begin, as well as setting up fallback dates and times just in case something strange happens. Both sides start the rite at around the same time, but it doesn't need to be exact. And during the forty to sixty plus minutes the rite takes, both sides will overlap significantly, and each side knows that they are overlapping because the pathstone looks a certain way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T13:13:53-08:00","id":1503699,"title":"","content":"The balance I think to strive for here, is that Moon Bridges shouldn't be harder, but they should be enough work that Septs have people dedicated to maintaining them as part of their jobs. It has to be enough effort (the pros of them are obvious IMO) that they're willing to take a Garou off the front lines and work a logistical job, without making it so difficult that Garou question that decision in &quot;normal&quot; circumstances. <br /> <br /> As Black Fox has pointed out, there are ways to handle this and to interpret the text to make sure you capture the tone here. And that's going to matter more to play than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T19:12:12-08:00","id":1503720,"title":"","content":"I suppose the Moonwalker office mentioned in Players Guide 2nd would be the emissary mentioned in Revised (or a pack of them). This office makes all the arrangements to establish new Moon Bridges. After that it's only a matter of following a schedule to renew them. Unfortunately Pathstones are not a very well developed fetish, but as Black Fox said this can be used in the favor of a ST wants.<br /> <br /> By what it's said in Caern Places of Power I think most of the problematic regarding time differences are handled by the caern totems involved. I imagine once the name of the sept and other info are known by the emissary/moonwalker they return and inform all the conditions to the Gatekeeper to synchronize with the other sept and the caern totem just answers to the Gatekeeper's call after the alliance terms have been established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","user":"Fenixpp","date":". 02-22-2023, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}